        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Manage Claw cron jobs through the gateway",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- install grouped Claw cron declarations through the gateway-owned `cron.add` API\n- persist pending, complete, failed, or removed ownership references keyed by final agent id and declaration id\n- expose cron ownership in status, round-trip complete declarations through export, and include exact cron state in remove consent\n- disable Claw-owned recurring work before canonical agent deletion, package cleanup, or workspace cleanup\n- reuse and extend the canonical agent deletion lifecycle without letting Claws delete unrelated agent files\n\n## Contract\n\n- scheduler mutation stays in the gateway; Claws never write the cron store directly\n- declaration keys are scoped as `claw:<agent-id>:<manifest-job-id>`, so package-local ids do not collide globally\n- response-lost retries reconcile by declaration key before issuing another `cron.add`\n- `main` declarations target `session:agent:<final-agent-id>:main`; `isolated` remains isolated, and strict v1 validation rejects other session modes\n- removal calls `cron.remove` before any agent/config mutation and records partial state if recurring work cannot be proven disabled\n- canonical `agents.delete` remains responsible for normal agent cleanup; Claws request config/session cleanup while retaining their narrowly managed workspace files for digest-aware removal\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27\n- Depends on: #102306 grouped export\n- This PR: gateway-owned cron mutation, provenance, status, export, and removal\n- Next: #102406 validated MCP ownership\n\nAll behavior remains gated by `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.test.src.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/test-src.tsbuildinfo`\n- 61 focused cron/lifecycle/schema/provenance/export unit tests\n- 15 Claws CLI tests\n- 11 canonical agent-delete command tests\n- 1 shared agent-cron cleanup test\n- 96 gateway agent-mutation tests across gateway projects\n- 8 full lifecycle CLI E2E tests\n- emitted `cron.add` payload validated by the gateway protocol validator\n- Oxlint: 0 warnings, 0 errors across 18 code/generated files\n- Oxfmt: all 18 files correctly formatted\n- `git diff --check`\n- Codex review: no accepted/actionable findings\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nThe lifecycle tests prove consent-bound add, scheduler-id provenance, response-lost reconciliation, status/export visibility, and removal ordering. A scheduler failure returns partial with `agentRemoved: false`; successful removal calls `cron.remove` before either direct config mutation or the canonical agent-delete delegate.\n",
